
---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'SEO Services | Top League Technologies',
  description:
    'SEO-led website development and practical search optimisation to help your business get found, understood and chosen.',
};

const enquiryLink =
  'mailto:hello@topleaguetech.com?subject=SEO%20Services%20Enquiry';
---

<Layout metadata={metadata} pageClass="product-description-page">

  <!-- 1. HERO -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow">
        <span class="dot"></span>
        SEO for website development
      </div>

      <h1>
        A Good Website Isn't Enough.
        <span>It Needs SEO Built In.</span>
      </h1>

      <p>
        We build SEO into your website from the planning stage. Already have a
        website? We'll identify what's holding it back and help put it right.
      </p>

      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn primary" href={enquiryLink}>Free consultation ↗</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href="#process">See how we do it ↓</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 2. THE SEO REALITY -->
  <section class="section band" id="story">
    <div class="container story-layout">
      <div class="story-content">
        <div class="kicker">The SEO reality</div>

        <h2>Poor SEO affecting your website?</h2>

        <p>
          Your website may look great, but poor SEO can make it harder for
          potential customers to find you, understand what you offer and take
          action.
        </p>

        <div class="process-list">
          <article class="step">
            <span>01</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Hard to find</h3>
              <p>
                Weak keyword targeting, poor indexing and technical issues
                can keep your pages out of relevant search results.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="step">
            <span>02</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Hard to understand</h3>
              <p>
                Poor page structure, unclear service descriptions and weak
                internal links make it harder for visitors and search engines
                to understand your business.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="step">
            <span>03</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Hard to convert</h3>
              <p>
                Even when visitors arrive, weak content, poor user experience
                and misplaced calls to action can cost you enquiries.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <p>
          <strong>
            And these problems aren't always visible on the surface.
          </strong>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 3. OUR APPROACH -->
  <section class="section" id="process">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="process">

        <div>
          <div class="kicker">Our approach</div>

          <h2>
            SEO starts before your website goes live.
          </h2>

          <p>
            A website shouldn't be built first and optimised as an
            afterthought. We bring SEO into the decisions that shape it —
            from what your pages say to how the whole site is put together.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="process-list">
          <article class="step">
            <span>01</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Research before design</h3>
              <p>
                We learn what your customers search for, what they need to
                know and which pages your business actually needs.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="step">
            <span>02</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Plan pages with purpose</h3>
              <p>
                We map services, topics, keywords and search intent into a
                clear page structure, navigation and URL plan.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="step">
            <span>03</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Build on solid foundations</h3>
              <p>
                We develop a fast, mobile-friendly site with clean structure,
                useful content, sensible internal links and technical SEO
                essentials.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="step">
            <span>04</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Check before launch</h3>
              <p>
                We review key pages, metadata, links, indexing settings,
                redirects and performance before the site is ready to meet
                the world.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 border-y border-slate-200 py-6 dark:border-slate-700">
        <div class="kicker">Then the website goes live</div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
          Launch is the starting line, not the finish.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 p-7 text-white dark:bg-slate-800 md:grid md:grid-cols-2 md:items-center md:gap-8">
        <div>
          <div class="kicker">After launch</div>
          <h3 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold">
            Keep learning. Keep improving.
          </h3>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-4 text-slate-300 md:mt-0">
          We monitor how the site performs, identify opportunities and refine
          content and SEO over time — because search visibility grows through
          ongoing work, not a one-off launch checklist.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-muted">
        The right starting point depends on your business, your audience and
        the website you need.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 4. SEO FOUNDATIONS -->
  <section class="section band" id="included">
    <div class="container">

      <div class="feature-head">
        <div>
          <div class="kicker">What we do</div>
          <h2>The SEO foundations every website needs.</h2>
        </div>

        <p>
          Good SEO isn't one setting or a collection of keywords. It comes
          from getting several important elements working together.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="process-list">
        <article class="step">
          <span>01</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Keyword and search intent research</h3>
            <p>
              We identify the searches that matter to your business and
              understand what people are looking for before deciding how your
              pages should address them.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="step">
          <span>02</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Clear site structure</h3>
            <p>
              We organise your pages, navigation, headings and internal links
              so visitors and search engines can understand how your website
              fits together.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="step">
          <span>03</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Useful, relevant content</h3>
            <p>
              We create and refine page content that answers customer
              questions, communicates your value and naturally incorporates
              relevant search terms.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="step">
          <span>04</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Technical SEO essentials</h3>
            <p>
              We take care of important technical considerations, including
              mobile usability, page performance, metadata, crawlability and
              indexability.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 5. EXISTING WEBSITES -->
  <section class="section" id="difference">
    <div class="container">

      <div class="feature-head">
        <div>
          <div class="kicker">Already have a website?</div>
          <h2>Let's make it work harder.</h2>
        </div>

        <p>
          You don't necessarily need a new website to improve your SEO. The
          right solution depends on what's already working — and what's
          holding it back.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="features">

        <article class="feature">
          <div>
            <div class="kicker">Targeted improvements</div>

            <h3>Improve what you already have.</h3>

            <p>
              If your website has a sound structure, we can focus on the areas
              that need attention.
            </p>

            <ul>
              <li>Review existing pages and search performance</li>
              <li>Improve content, headings and metadata</li>
              <li>Fix internal linking and on-page SEO issues</li>
              <li>Address technical problems affecting visibility</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="feature">
          <div>
            <div class="kicker">A stronger foundation</div>

            <h3>Restructure or rebuild when needed.</h3>

            <p>
              Sometimes the underlying website is the problem. A more
              substantial change may be the better long-term investment.
            </p>

            <ul>
              <li>Reorganise confusing site structures</li>
              <li>Rework pages that fail to serve their purpose</li>
              <li>Improve design, usability and performance</li>
              <li>Build a better website with SEO at its core</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-muted">
        We start by understanding your website and identifying what it
        actually needs — not by assuming that a rebuild is always the answer.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 6. ONGOING SEO -->
  <section class="section band" id="why">
    <div class="container">

      <div class="feature-head">
        <div>
          <div class="kicker">After launch</div>
          <h2>SEO doesn't stop when your website goes live.</h2>
        </div>

        <p>
          A launch gives your website a strong starting point. Growing its
          visibility takes attention, useful content and improvements guided
          by how people actually find and use it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="story-content">
        <p>
          Search behaviour changes. Your business evolves. And the pages that
          matter most today may not be the ones that bring in your next
          customer.
        </p>

        <p>
          That is why SEO needs to continue after launch. We look at what is
          working, where people are dropping off and which opportunities are
          worth acting on.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>
            No guesswork or endless changes for the sake of it. The next step
            should be based on what the website needs.
          </strong>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="process-list mt-10">

        <article class="step">
          <span>01</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Monitor search performance</h3>
            <p>
              Track visibility, relevant search queries and the pages
              attracting attention.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="step">
          <span>02</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Improve important pages</h3>
            <p>
              Refine page content, titles, structure and internal links as
              needs become clearer.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="step">
          <span>03</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Find the next opportunities</h3>
            <p>
              Identify useful topics, content gaps and pages your audience
              still needs.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="step">
          <span>04</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Keep the site in good shape</h3>
            <p>
              Address technical issues and make sure the foundations continue
              to support the site.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 7. FINAL CTA -->
  <section id="contact" class="cta">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="kicker">Let's get started</div>

      <h2>
        Ready to build a website that works harder for your business?
      </h2>

      <p>
        Whether you're planning a new website or want to get more from the one
        you already have, let's talk about what would make the biggest
        difference.
      </p>

      <a class="btn primary" href={enquiryLink}>
        Book a free consultation ↗
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
